<details>
<summary><h2>✨ Features</h2></summary>

- 📷 Automated screenshot capturing  
- ⏱ Flexible time intervals (hours, minutes, seconds)  
- 📁 Auto directory creation  
- 🖥 OS-level screen capture  
- ⛔ Graceful exit using keyboard interrupt  
- 🔧 Simple CLI interface  

</details>

---

<details>
<summary><h2>⚙️ Installation</h2></summary>

```bash
pip install pyautogui
```

- System Requirements

- Python 3.x

- OS with GUI (Windows / Linux / macOS)


</details>

---

<details>
<summary><h2>🚀 Usage</h2></summary>

```
python screenshot.py -p ./images -t m -f 2
```

This captures 2 screenshots per minute and stores them in ./images.

</details>

---

<details>
<summary><h2>🧩 CLI Arguments</h2></summary>

Argument	Description	Default

```
-p, --path	Directory to save screenshots	./images
-t, --type	Time unit (h, m, s)	h
-f, --frequency	Screenshots per unit	1
```

</details>

---

<details>
<summary><h2>🧠 Internal Working</h2></summary>

- Parses CLI arguments using argpa

- Convert time units into second

- Ensures minimum delay of 1 sec

- Create seats directory if missing

- Enters infinite loop:

- Captures screenshot

- Names file using current timestamp

- Saves image

- Sleeps until next capture



</details>

